{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons","id":1480630,"title":"[2e] List of Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-09T21:07:28-07:00","id":1480630,"title":"[2e] List of Pantheons","content":"So something that I've been looking for and haven't really found is a comprehensive list of the pantheons actually mentioned (with full write-ups or just mentions) in Scion. So I thought I'd put one together myself. If there's any that someone else caught and I didn't, let me know so I can fill it in. I haven't included ones talked about by the devs either, mostly because I don't remember where/when they talked about them. Again, if anyone does remember, please let me know.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Full Write-ups</span><br /> <b>Hero</b><br /> -The Aesir of Asgard and Midgard<br /> -The Dev\u00e1 of South Asia<br /> -The Kami of Japan<br /> -The Manitou of the Anishinaabek<br /> -The Netjer of Egypt<br /> -The \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 of Yor\u00f9b\u00e1land<br /> -The Sh\u00e9n of China<br /> -The Te\u014dtl of M\u0113xihcah<br /> -The Theoi of Greece and Rome<br /> -The Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann of Ireland<br /> <b>Mysteries of the World</b><br /> -The Loa of Haiti<br /> -The Nemetondevos of Gaul<br /> -The Teros of Atlantis (Fictional)<br /> -The Yazata of Persia<br /> <b>Demigod</b><br /> -The Anunna of Mesopotamia<br /> -The Apu of the Inca<br /> -The Atua of Polynesia<br /> -The Bogovi of the Slavs<br /> -The Tengri of Mongolia<br /> <b>God</b><br /> -The Balahala of Visayas<br /> -The Ilhm of Phoenicia<br /> -The K'uh of the Maya<br /> -The P\u0101las of Buddhism<br /> -The Zem\u00ed of the Ta\u00edno<br /> <b>Once and Future</b><br /> -The Plant Don of Wales<br /> <br /> <b>Masks of the Mythos</b><br /> -The Elder Gods of the Mythos (Fictional)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mentioned</span><br /> -The Kalou-Vu of Fiji<br /> -The Kamuy of the Ainu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","user":"kamenhero25","date":". 07-31-2023, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T23:20:13-07:00","id":1480635,"title":"","content":"The Kalou-Vu of Fiji are mentioned in the Scion: Dragons manuscript<br /> <br /> obviously the Mythos pantheon in Masks of the Mythos would be another fictional one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T02:44:30-07:00","id":1480644,"title":"","content":"Looking at the list and putting the gods on a mental map I see some gaps. The western US and Canada aren't there. Africa is vast but only Egypt and Southern Nigeria are covered. Indonesia, specifically Bali has it own take on the Devas. It's every bit as distinct as the Loa/Orisha divide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T09:19:56-07:00","id":1480668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480644#post1480644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the list and putting the gods on a mental map I see some gaps. The western US and Canada aren't there. Africa is vast but only Egypt and Southern Nigeria are covered. Indonesia, specifically Bali has it own take on the Devas. It's every bit as distinct as the Loa/Orisha divide.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes these are the only ones that have been gotten to yet in official publications. There is plenty of room for growth still. But one major factor is making sure they do it ethically and not exploit information that continuous living traditions did not choose to share for use in fiction by outsiders, which is a major issue with indigenous American and Australian pantheons in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T11:26:00-07:00","id":1480678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480668#post1480668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yes these are the only ones that have been gotten to yet in official publications. There is plenty of room for growth still. But one major factor is making sure they do it ethically and not exploit information that continuous living traditions did not choose to share for use in fiction by outsiders, which is a major issue with indigenous American and Australian pantheons in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to what standards they set for getting permission on that kind of thing, especially in the case of religions that lack a centralized authority that can speak on behalf of all adherents.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T13:55:29-07:00","id":1480688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480678#post1480678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious as to what standards they set for getting permission on that kind of thing, especially in the case of religions that lack a centralized authority that can speak on behalf of all adherents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since obviously you can\u2019t get permission from all adherents, the general rule of thumb as I understand it is consultation if not writer from the given culture. That\u2019s not a high bar but in several cases it\u2019s still not surmountable because either these stories are sacred secrets, or they\u2019ve been really badly burned by white anthropologists or writers who lied to them in the past, etc. and in those cases the correct response is \u201cok we will respect that and move on\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T15:52:04-07:00","id":1480699,"title":"","content":"Let me make a comment, while all the other Pantheons are described as *gods* from *place in the World*, the Aesir are Aesir from Midgard. It should be Aesir from Scandinavia or Norsemann.<br /> I know its like this in the book too, but it disturb me a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T17:39:40-07:00","id":1480706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480668#post1480668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yes these are the only ones that have been gotten to yet in official publications. There is plenty of room for growth still. But one major factor is making sure they do it ethically and not exploit information that continuous living traditions did not choose to share for use in fiction by outsiders, which is a major issue with indigenous American and Australian pantheons in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the information is in standard scholarly resources, and there has been no controversy, the point is moot. And if it isn't, your saying that it is evil to play this game period. <br /> <br /> I point blank reject the idea that this game is evil. As long as the depiction of the pantheons are respectful and reasonably accurate they can be included. <br /> <br /> Let's not be like the people who, knowing nothing about &quot;Kimba the White Lion&quot; go around proclaiming that Disney's &quot;The Lion King&quot; is a mere copy of Kimba. Any comparison of the two would show that neither is a copy of the other and all similarities come from the African setting and the ancient motif of Lions as animal kings. But many people scream racism and demand that Disney give all its profits on the movie to the company that owns Kimba.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the son of the man who created Kimba is offended that the controversy exists. He feels that his father's achievements are being down rated and ignored because of the controversy. And they are, the creator of &quot;Kimba, the White Lion&quot; had massive influence on both Manga and Anime. But the Kimba/Lion King controversy reduced him from a major creator on the level of Disney himself to a mere victim needing white saviors.<br /> <br /> Let's not make the same kind of belittling mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T18:25:53-07:00","id":1480709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480706#post1480706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the information is in standard scholarly resources, and there has been no controversy, the point is moot. And if it isn't, your saying that it is evil to play this game period. <br /> <br /> I point blank reject the idea that this game is evil. As long as the depiction of the pantheons are respectful and reasonably accurate they can be included. </div> </div> </div> </div>Depicting some sacred traditions for the entertainment of outsiders are not capable of being respectful, because cultures are not all the same, and some of them are not as open as others for outsiders. You may be comfortable violating that all you like at your table, but the Scion developers don\u2019t feel doing so for mass consumption and profit is an ethical thing to do.<br /> <br /> If members of the given culture are as comfortable with it as you assume than OPP will have no problem finding writers and consultants. If they consistently say no, \u201cactually I\u2019m belittling your culture if I ignore your wishes you are explicitly telling me\u201d doesn\u2019t carry the water you think it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T19:09:32-07:00","id":1480712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480644#post1480644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the list and putting the gods on a mental map I see some gaps. The western US and Canada aren't there. Africa is vast but only Egypt and Southern Nigeria are covered. Indonesia, specifically Bali has it own take on the Devas. It's every bit as distinct as the Loa/Orisha divide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Navajo, Inuit, Australian Aboriginal, and Canaanite have been mentioned by the devs before, though I only actually listed ones that are in books or manuscripts right now. I would be interested to see more African cultures explored certainly, as well as Southeast Asian outside of just India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T19:34:45-07:00","id":1480714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480712#post1480712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that Navajo, Inuit, Australian Aboriginal, and Canaanite have been mentioned by the devs before, though I only actually listed ones that are in books or manuscripts right now. I would be interested to see more African cultures explored certainly, as well as Southeast Asian outside of just India.</div> </div> </div> </div>Confirmed for God: Visayan, Taino, and Canaanite. The other two are not confirmed yet, though the Pal\u0101s (Vajrayana Buddhist) have been seeded a great deal, as have the K\u2019uh (Maya), so those would be my top two guesses, though if they get an Apachean pantheon that would be fantastic!<br /> <br /> i haven\u2019t heard anything about Aboriginal Australian from OPP, but there was a fan from that background who was working on something potentially for the Nexus.<br /> <br /> in terms of fan works there are some great Vietnamese, Thai, Burmese, Haida, Choctaw, Akan, Hittite, and Manchu pantheons floating about, not even counting the stuff on the Nexus (Theosophic, modern Venezuelan, and Guarani being the ones I\u2019m aware of there), as well alternate takes on the Nemetondevos and the Taino Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-10-2022, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T19:38:56-07:00","id":1480715,"title":"","content":"You could honestly do Hero-sized sourcebooks about each individual pantheon and still not cover every possible thing about them. <br /> <br /> I think we're supposed to get the Welsh in the forthcoming Arthurian book (Once &amp; Future, IIRC). And I'd guess (hopefully) five more pantheons in the God book. I couldn't begin to guess which ones those might be. I would enjoy seeing something from southern Africa though. And possibly Korea. <br /> <br /> Maybe we'll be lucky enough to get something akin to Mysteries of The World for DemiGod and God which also include a few more. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T20:01:25-07:00","id":1480718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480715#post1480715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could honestly do Hero-sized sourcebooks about each individual pantheon and still not cover every possible thing about them.<br /> <br /> I think we're supposed to get the Welsh in the forthcoming Arthurian book (Once &amp; Future, IIRC). And I'd guess (hopefully) five more pantheons in the God book. I couldn't begin to guess which ones those might be. I would enjoy seeing something from southern Africa though. And possibly Korea.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll be lucky enough to get something akin to Mysteries of The World for DemiGod and God which also include a few more.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Scion Demigod Companion on the list of stuff they have in development on Kickstarter, so I would assume God will get one as well. Frankly, I also wouldn't be opposed to a book that's just like 150 pages of new gods/pantheons and nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T20:57:53-07:00","id":1480721,"title":"","content":"At some point I would enjoy seeing something similar to the Loa vis a vis the Orisha with the German/Saxon version of the Aesir and the Roman version of the Theoi. Maybe also the Carthage version of the Canaanites if that is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:23:02-07:00","id":1480724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480721#post1480721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point I would enjoy seeing something similar to the Loa vis a vis the Orisha with the German/Saxon version of the Aesir and the Roman version of the Theoi. Maybe also the Carthage version of the Canaanites if that is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>there\u2019s definitely enough info to support a full writeup for the Dei. They definitely can support their own Virtue pairing (Stoicism and Virtus) and PSP (the Metamorphosis stories all being very much rebranded or reinvented Greek narratives rather than indigenous Romans ones)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T06:41:12-07:00","id":1480742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480715#post1480715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could honestly do Hero-sized sourcebooks about each individual pantheon and still not cover every possible thing about them. <br /> <br /> I think we're supposed to get the Welsh in the forthcoming Arthurian book (Once &amp; Future, IIRC). And I'd guess (hopefully) five more pantheons in the God book. I couldn't begin to guess which ones those might be. I would enjoy seeing something from southern Africa though. And possibly Korea. <br /> <br /> Maybe we'll be lucky enough to get something akin to Mysteries of The World for DemiGod and God which also include a few more. </div> </div> </div> </div>True! But it would be worthwhile to do sourcebooks for some of the pantheons more likely to sell. Do the Greek, Norse, Egyptian, and Irish, pantheons first. Then hope you have the profits to finance more pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T11:12:25-07:00","id":1480752,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really looking forward to seeing the Canaanite pantheon in God. Enough so that I\u2019d be willing to back it even if they moved to IndieGoGo rather than Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T11:40:43-07:00","id":1480756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480709#post1480709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depicting some sacred traditions for the entertainment of outsiders are not capable of being respectful, because cultures are not all the same, and some of them are not as open as others for outsiders. You may be comfortable violating that all you like at your table, but the Scion developers don\u2019t feel doing so for mass consumption and profit is an ethical thing to do.<br /> <br /> If members of the given culture are as comfortable with it as you assume than OPP will have no problem finding writers and consultants. If they consistently say no, \u201cactually I\u2019m belittling your culture if I ignore your wishes you are explicitly telling me\u201d doesn\u2019t carry the water you think it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mainly want a fight. Go elsewhere I won't give you one. <br /> <br /> I will put forth a simple argument. We already have an example of a pantheon for a living faith. The Devas represent the third largest faith on Earth. <br /> <br /> Although my knowledge of the peoples and cultures of South Asia does have serious limits it's clear that, although the vast majority would have no issue with our game, a small minority, twenty million or so, would call Scion a blasphemy. Are you ready to remove the Devas from the game?<br /> <br /> My question is rhetorical, I won't answer you on this question again. I respect the rules of these boards and distain sandbagging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T15:34:15-07:00","id":1480766,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>General Request for the thread to cool down, please. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T16:14:28-07:00","id":1480772,"title":"","content":"Back to the topic. <br /> <br /> Just as this game has done the Loas, looking at their profound links with the Orishas, I think the Devas as seen through the lens of Balinese Hindu-Buddhist syncretic mythology would be fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T05:12:02-07:00","id":1480823,"title":"","content":"We already get a taste of that in Titanomachy with Rangda and discussion of Barong. Plus brief mention of Durga's perception in Bali and her relationship with Rangda, and how Indra, Vishnu and Karttikeya defer to Barong when they visit Bali. A full sub-pantheon/exploration of that would be interesting to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","user":"demonchilde","date":". 05-12-2022, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T08:50:38-07:00","id":1480836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480724#post1480724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> there\u2019s definitely enough info to support a full writeup for the Dei. They definitely can support their own Virtue pairing (Stoicism and Virtus) and PSP (the Metamorphosis stories all being very much rebranded or reinvented Greek narratives rather than indigenous Romans ones)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dei Scent of the Divine: the smell of boiling wine with saffron covering up shit and blood [i.e. the smell of the Colosseum] and the distant sound of a Legion\u2019s war trumpets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T09:12:54-07:00","id":1480838,"title":"","content":"I think the Roman Dei would smell olive, maybe covering shit and blood. The Romans didn\u2019t use soap, their technique was covering themselves with olive oil and removing it with a stick before bathing in hot water, so olive covering shit and blood would be perfect description of Roman smell.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Dei x Theoi, there is one great CC called Imperium ( <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325650/Imperium\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325650/Imperium</a> ), it\u2019s not a book about the main gods of Roman pantheon, but about the gods that are not part of the Greek tradition and matter to the Romans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T16:18:00-07:00","id":1480881,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that the Kachinas would be a truly interesting group to do on several levels.<br /> <br /> First the status of the different Kachinas has interesting ins and outs. Some are clearly gods, others are closer to what Westerners would call fairies. Still others are more like ghosts becoming gods. The Kachina would need a defined ability to turn ghosts into gods just like the Shen. <br /> <br /> Another aspect that would be fascinating is that the Hopi and Zunni are hyper-traditionalists that are well adapted to the modern world. Thus the pantheon would have many interesting ways to get into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T17:02:48-07:00","id":1480893,"title":"","content":"I'll have to double-check to make sure; but isn't it possible for <i>any</i> God to (eventually) make a ghost into a god? As far as I know, there's nothing saying that ghosts can't be Chosen as Scions. Ditto with Immortals, for that matter: I believe that just about <i>anyone</i> can be Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T01:05:35-07:00","id":1480945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480893#post1480893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to double-check to make sure; but isn't it possible for <i>any</i> God to (eventually) make a ghost into a god? As far as I know, there's nothing saying that ghosts can't be Chosen as Scions. Ditto with Immortals, for that matter: I believe that just about <i>anyone</i> can be Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a bit of a pain to get people like Hel and Ereshkigal to let go of one of their charges to let you turn them into Scion. I mean, you could, but there are much easier ways to get scions so it seems like a 'only done under super special circumstances' kind of thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T09:16:54-07:00","id":1480968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480756#post1480756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will put forth a simple argument. We already have an example of a pantheon for a living faith. The Devas represent the third largest faith on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they had consultants for the Deva in Scion 2E. Samudra has commented on this forum before discussing that role. It's part of why that write up is as good as it is! Which is exactly what they should have for any other pantheon based on a continuous living tradition. I never suggested that a minority should get to veto the inclusion of a pantheon if they have willing consultants/writers from that culture. I said that if they can't find consultants because people from that culture consistently say &quot;no&quot;, then they should respect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-13-2022, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T12:03:39-07:00","id":1480984,"title":"","content":"Eh, I actually kinda felt like their write up was a bit biased by acting like they were the best thanks to having a bunch of WMDs laying around that 'maybe' some other pantheons very best named weapons like Mjolnir could counter. I'm not sure if it is lore accurate to the original religion or not but from a balance standpoint stressing how many divine nuclear weapons they have compared to the others seems odd. On the other hand, they weren't afraid to make them look bad when it comes to their war hawk attitude about Titans so maybe it balances out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T12:24:43-07:00","id":1480988,"title":"","content":"I'd enjoy seeing things like the Finns or Lithuanians, but I have odd tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T14:22:41-07:00","id":1481009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480945#post1480945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably a bit of a pain to get people like Hel and Ereshkigal to let go of one of their charges to let you turn them into Scion. I mean, you could, but there are much easier ways to get scions so it seems like a 'only done under super special circumstances' kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that would depend on the Pantheon. My thought is that mythologies where ghosts often become gods have Pantheons where the gods of the dead aren't nearly so possessive of their charges. You wouldn't see that sorry of thing happening all that often with the likes of the Theoi or Aesir; but Astromancer's proposed Kachinas Pantheon could be presented as an exception where the dead are often Chosen, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T17:18:40-07:00","id":1481028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1481009#post1481009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that would depend on the Pantheon. My thought is that mythologies where ghosts often become gods have Pantheons where the gods of the dead aren't nearly so possessive of their charges. You wouldn't see that sorry of thing happening all that often with the likes of the Theoi or Aesir; but Astromancer's proposed Kachinas Pantheon could be presented as an exception where the dead are often Chosen, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it will vary a bit. Apparently Hades will let someone go if you just play him a kickass music solo, for example. But I think more often then not mythologies didn't look kindly on dead people leaving their designated dead people places to go get a second chance at life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T20:38:01-07:00","id":1481043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1480988#post1480988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd enjoy seeing things like the Finns or Lithuanians, but I have odd tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they'd be great choices. Their obscurity would be an issue for them especially trapped between two of the most famous pantheons (Norse and Greek). Also it's established in game that both of those pantheons are aggressive towards their more obscure neighbors. Finnish and Baltic deities would be under serious pressure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T01:36:55-07:00","id":1481051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1481043#post1481043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they'd be great choices. Their obscurity would be an issue for them especially trapped between two of the most famous pantheons (Norse and Greek). Also it's established in game that both of those pantheons are aggressive towards their more obscure neighbors. Finnish and Baltic deities would be under serious pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bogovi have some of that going on already. They in an interesting spot. I would definitely be interested in more of that general region, though I know very little about Finnish mythology. Or Eastern European in general really. It gets a bit blotted out being between two titans of modern cultural attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:19:38-07:00","id":1481077,"title":"","content":"Well, Norse and Greco-Roman mythology are much better documented than, say, Slavic mythology or any of the other pagan mythological beliefs of Europe. The only other one that comes close is Irish mythology and what we have of that went through a process of reinterpretation and reinvention by the Christian monks who recorded it. Indeed, a lot of what we &quot;know&quot; about Slavic mythology is wrong, the unintentional creation of Victorian folklorists misinterpreting what little data they had.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm surprised that there hasn't been a write-up of Finnish mythology. Thanks to The Kalevala, it's better documented than many other European pagan belief systems; and it has more prominence than some pantheons that have been covered, such as the Mongolian one. Not nearly so well documented or so prominent as Norse and Greek myths, of course, but still, it seems like a more obvious candidate for a write up than some of the pantheons that have been covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T13:28:05-07:00","id":1481114,"title":"","content":"If I were to have a short list of unannounced pantheons I would like to see, it would probably be (in no particular order):<ul><li>Muskogee</li> <li>Finnish</li> <li>Inuit</li> <li>Hittites</li> <li>Choctaw/Chickasaw</li> <li>Bantu</li> <li>Vietnam</li> <li>Ainu</li> </ul>The longer list would include stuff like Korea, Fiji, Maori, Basque, the full Iroquois, Mayan, Ainu, Arabian, Cherokee, and some of the native pantheons of Columbia, Brazil, and Argentina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-14-2022, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:06:24-07:00","id":1481118,"title":"","content":"The mythology of the San people of Southern Africa seems like it would be an interesting choice. Their chief god is a trickster figure, the Mantis (as in, the insect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T09:44:39-07:00","id":1481183,"title":"","content":"If I were to have my own wish list, it would be:<br /> * Bon<br /> * Cherokee<br /> * Finnish<br /> * Inuit<br /> * Iroquois (beyond the brief write-up two of their gods get in the Manitou pantheon)<br /> * Lakota<br /> * Mayan<br /> * San<br /> * Tibetan Buddhist<br /> <br /> It seems likely that the Mayan and Tibetan Buddhist gods will be forthcoming at some point.<br /> <br /> I would have added Hopi and Navajo, but we already know those are no-gos because of opposition from members of those peoples.<br /> <br /> I would do the Bon (the gods of Tibet's native shamanic tradition) as sharing virtues and a PSP with the Tibetan Buddhist deities, but being their own separate pantheon, with their own distinct cosmology.<br /> <br /> And I'm also sure there's pantheons out there I know little or nothing about that would make for interesting inclusions, like one or more of the Australian Aboriginal peoples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T09:48:12-07:00","id":1481185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1481114#post1481114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The longer list would include stuff like Korea, Fiji, Maori, Basque, the full Iroquois, Mayan, Ainu, Arabian, Cherokee, and some of the native pantheons of Columbia, Brazil, and Argentina.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maori pantheon is written up on Demigod. They're referred to as Polynesian, but they focused on the Maori understanding of those deities, with a note that other Polynesian pantheons can be considered mantles of those same gods; plus they added in Pele from Hawaii.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T11:20:51-07:00","id":1481306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480630-2e-list-of-pantheons?p=1481028#post1481028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, it will vary a bit. Apparently Hades will let someone go if you just play him a kickass music solo, for example. But I think more often then not mythologies didn't look kindly on dead people leaving their designated dead people places to go get a second chance at life.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMore often than not\u201d, sure. But I'm specifically suggesting making one Pantheon the exception to that guideline: they would be the \u201cnot\u201d in the \u201cmore often than not\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}